    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Protocol 04</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Review the car's performance, ensuring all systems (engine, suspension, brakes, etc.) are functioning properly.</p>
  </div>
</div>

	<p>To ensure accurate mileage tracking and prevent any discrepancies, we must verify the vehicle's odometer reading against the Load Receipt (LR) bill of lading.</p>
	<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Compare the displayed odometer reading on the destination vehicle with the one recorded on the LR bill of lading.</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>If the odometer reading on the destination vehicle matches the recorded reading on the LR bill of lading, no further action is required.</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>If there is a discrepancy, document the difference and obtain the consignee's signature on the LR bill of lading for verification.</span></li>
	</ul>

	<p>To ensure transparency and accountability, we must obtain a signed condition sign-off from the consignee or authorized representative.</p>
	<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Have the consignee or representative inspect the vehicle and confirm its condition.</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Provide the consignee with a copy of the pickup photos taken during the initial inspection.</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Require the consignee to sign and date the condition report, acknowledging the vehicle's condition during delivery.</span></li>
	</ul>
	<p>It is essential to document any discrepancies or damages observed during the re-inspection and include them in the signed condition report.</p>
	<p>Upon receiving the signed condition sign-off, the consignee confirms that they have inspected the vehicle and are satisfied with its condition at the destination.</p>
	<p>This process ensures a transparent and accurate documentation of the vehicle's condition, preventing potential disputes or claim issues later on.</p>
	<p>If any discrepancies are found during the re-inspection, they should be listed in detail on the signed condition report alongside clear photos taken at the destination.</p>
	<p>By completing this process, we aim to provide peace of mind to both parties and ensure a smooth and satisfactory delivery experience for the consignee.</p></div>
